17592186498379 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498379 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498379 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2add9653-97c2-5314-8eb6-5cd64b3d830e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "594aa2c5-6ab3-59e0-94ef-12b55bd75a5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=6.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ and ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "023c52b0-f119-5895-8d3f-31a9468a20b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $4,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $4$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\  & =-4det(A) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1071 "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2, \\\\ {2}^{xy},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<3,\\,0<y<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(-1,3)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c17f34a-606d-54c2-a49c-4cce7dcaf8e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498492 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =((-1,1)\\cup (1,3))\\times (0,2) \\\\  & =((-1,1)\\times (0,2))\\cup ((1,3)\\times (0,2)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,3)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,3)\\times (0,2)}{2}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=4xy\\,i+(2{x}^{2}+2yz)\\,j+({y}^{2}+1)\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "556e4e71-69c2-58ca-8978-843d74c13525" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498537 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+2yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2{x}^{2}+2yz \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 2yz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{2}z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)={y}^{2}z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+1 & ={y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =1 \\\\ h(z) & =z+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+z+C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0f7f665e-6a64-51bb-995b-e3a8d6ce7d2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498609 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498609 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "10c837f4-3881-5f94-911e-e3ff56ee65c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498609 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498612 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498612 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c164545-5826-5a3e-806d-b0dc3b18d6d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498612 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186437272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498622 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e6ea2d9-94f3-582a-af54-8a84e901dd4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498622 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498646 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498646 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b56955ce-7d3d-51f9-aa6c-775bc47e70ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498646 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186290423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498660 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498660 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fb66811b-e2d4-56e3-a240-443861ad0b1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498660 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186247250 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
